      "tree": {
        "sha": "9a24859326885eff53776325127dc85e3dd0b0c5",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/9a24859326885eff53776325127dc85e3dd0b0c5"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 9a24859326885eff53776325127dc85e3dd0b0c5\nparent 3efb4e7082f73eaa103a1c62376b1b7d9b4b53da\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1790221135 -0700\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1790231827 -0700\n\ninit: drain callbacks before saving fee estimates\n\nShutdown saves fee estimates before draining queued validation callbacks.\nA queued block update can leave the saved mined-block stats behind the chain tip, so they are ignored on restart.\n\nSave and unregister the estimator after the existing callback drain.\nRemove the stale comment claiming the drain only lets the wallet catch up, since wallets are unloaded at the start of shutdown.\nIncoming IPC clients remain connected until later in shutdown and need separate handling.\n",
